(7666504, 1250357, 28742, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by glad2badad:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m a bit of a nit-picker and thought that 1) the board &amp; pieces could have been cleaned prior to taking the photo, and 2) turn the pawns so the seam of the plastic pieces don''t show.<br/>For the allegory to work perhaps a white king and black pawns would have sold the concept better, unless I''m out in left field and missing the point. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I think what Barry is trying to say is that your chess set is cheap and also he''s a racist. :P</td>', 'Originally posted by glad2badad: I''m a bit of a nit-picker and thought that 1) the board & pieces could have been cleaned prior to taking the photo, and 2) turn the pawns so the seam of the plastic pieces don''t show.For the allegory to work perhaps a white king and black pawns would have sold the concept better, unless I''m out in left field and missing the point.   I think what Barry is trying to say is that your chess set is cheap and also he''s a racist. :P', '2020-06-17 00:58:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(7666751, 1250423, 251422, '<td valign="top">Love the little people. Nice job Lydia!<br/></td>', 'Love the little people. Nice job Lydia!', '2020-06-18 13:00:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(7667099, 1250543, 19825, '<td valign="top">When you enter a less traditional image, sometimes the best you can hope for is to connect with a handful of voters. An 8 and a couple of 9s shows you did. However, with a less traditional image you are more likely to have a few low votes. It is really hard to recover from votes of 2 and 3. A thought that might be helpful for you to keep in mind.</td>', 'When you enter a less traditional image, sometimes the best you can hope for is to connect with a handful of voters. An 8 and a couple of 9s shows you did. However, with a less traditional image you are more likely to have a few low votes. It is really hard to recover from votes of 2 and 3. A thought that might be helpful for you to keep in mind.', '2020-06-19 16:32:23.000000', NULL, 0);
COMMIT;
